  "summary": "The Alameda, California city council unanimously rejected a proposed $500,000 contract to purchase ALPR technology from Vigilant Solutions, citing the vendor's data-sharing arrangement with ICE. The ACLU framed the vote as a win for immigrants' rights and called on other cities to adopt surveillance oversight ordinances.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "the city of Alameda, California unanimously withheld approval of a proposed $500,000 contract to purchase license plate reader technology from Vigilant, a company that recently sold Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) access to its nationwide database.",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    },
    {
      "quote": "Under the reported agreement with Vigilant , ICE would be capable of accessing data collected by Vigilant from local law enforcement and private sources.",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "Alameda voted to send the city attorney and police back to the drawing board.",
